<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bomi Hills</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bomi Hills is an iron ore district in north-western Liberia, in present-day Bomi County. Mining by the Liberia Mining Company began there in 1951, making it the country's first iron mine, and its exports helped make Liberia one of the world's fastest-growing economies in the 1950s before the deposits were worked out.</p></div>
